FILE refs/src/flint-3.0.1/ulong_extras.rst sha256=65d6805bd89f8d66bf87f459d4f604b19499e5c9129896a07c72e11d4f773468
RANGE 456-458
456: .. function:: int n_jacobi(mp_limb_signed_t x, ulong y)
457: 
458:     Computes the Jacobi symbol `\left(\frac{x}{y}\right)` for any `x` and odd `y`.
FILE refs/src/flint-3.0.1/arb.rst sha256=2296237bf12759a183eb7e73e5d5e478c13a70ca465c16134193fbfe7cbaf973
RANGE 285-298
285: .. function:: char * arb_dump_str(const arb_t x)
286: 
287:     Returns a serialized representation of *x* as a null-terminated
288:     ASCII string that can be read by :func:`arb_load_str`. The format consists
289:     of four hexadecimal integers representing the midpoint mantissa,
290:     midpoint exponent, radius mantissa and radius exponent (with special
291:     values to indicate zero, infinity and NaN values),
292:     separated by single spaces. The returned string needs to be deallocated
293:     with *flint_free*.
294: 
295: .. function:: int arb_load_str(arb_t x, const char * str)
296: 
297:     Sets *x* to the serialized representation given in *str*. Returns a
298:     nonzero value if *str* is not formatted correctly (see :func:`arb_dump_str`).
